# tools/ales_stereo_center_clip_witness.rish — stereo_center_clip: the center clipper carried into stereo with ONE SHARED DEAD ZONE, both channels in lockstep, opening the dead-zone corner of the stereo NONLINEAR
# class (ALES141).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES141.
# Design read: active-designing/20260815-042021_fill-ales141-lotus-stereo-center-clip.md
# Stands on: lotus/center_clip.rye (ALES87 — the mono center clipper run once per channel, y = if |x| ≤ t then 0 else x with no rail edge), lotus/stereo_crush.rye (ALES136 — the not-odd sibling whose
# antisymmetry-break this rung mirrors by HOLDING it), lotus/pan.rye (ALES10 — the StereoClip, two mono Clips left/right, and its balance invariant), lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 — the Clip, its buf/len/samples,
# sample_min/max). A Lotus master is a StereoClip whose defining invariant is that left and right hold the same length. This rung carries ALES87's dead zone into stereo — silencing the quiet middle and passing the
# loud in both channels, one dead zone landing on both speakers together. Where the hard clip caps the loud extremes, the center clip hollows the quiet middle; run together in stereo they keep only the band between
# the noise floor and the ceiling. Unlike the crush and tube, the center clipper is odd, so the same dead zone holds the inter-channel antisymmetry — an out-of-phase master comes back still out of phase.
#
# lotus/stereo_center_clip.rye validates both channels once against the shared threshold and length before either is mutated (BadThreshold on a threshold outside [0, sample_max], BadRange on a span outside the
# samples), then center-clips both channels through ALES87's center_clip; CenterClipError reused whole. The crux is four laws. THE STEREO CENTER-CLIP LAW: each channel equals ALES87's mono center_clip with the same
# threshold byte for byte. THE BALANCE / LENGTH LAW: left.len == right.len after, both holding their starting length. THE PER-CHANNEL ODD LAW: the antisymmetry holds under the shared dead zone (an out-of-phase master
# staying out of phase), every output 0 or its input, the map idempotent, the ratio held on the passed samples, an identical-channel master staying identical, thresh 0 the identity. THE ATOMICITY / DEGENERATE LAW: a
# refusal leaves both channels untouched and balanced, thresh 0 the identity, count 0 the identity.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ales_stereo_center_clip_witness.rish

say "ales-stereo-center-clip: Language EN — stereo_center_clip center-clips a span in both channels of a stereo master with the same threshold, silencing every sample whose magnitude is at most the threshold and passing every louder sample unchanged, the same dead zone on each, so one center clip lands on both speakers together. A Lotus master is two Clips heard together, one per speaker, whose defining invariant is that left and right hold the same length so the two channels stay aligned in time. This rung opens the dead-zone corner of the stereo nonlinear class on ALES87's center clipper, running the proven mono center clip on each channel with the same threshold, validated once against the shared threshold and length before either channel is mutated so a refusal never center-clips one channel and leaves the other whole."
say "ales-stereo-center-clip: Style Radiant — where ALES132's hard clip caps the loud extremes at a ceiling, the center clip hollows the quiet middle below a floor, and run together in stereo they keep only the band between the noise floor and the ceiling. Unlike ALES136's crush and ALES135's tube, which are not odd and break the inter-channel antisymmetry, the center clipper is odd, because the dead-zone map is symmetric about zero: the magnitude of minus x equals the magnitude of x, so the center clip of minus x equals minus the center clip of x. An out-of-phase master, right the exact negation of left, center-clipped through the same threshold comes back still out of phase, right still the negation of left — the odd law made stereo where the not-odd siblings broke it. A one-to-two master keeps its ratio on the passed samples, both silenced together in the dead zone and both passed together above it, and an identical-channel master stays identical. The rule is stated positively: the center clip is exact for every i16 with no rail edge and no saturate, the only values written being zero and the untouched input; it carries one parameter, the threshold magnitude, and names two faults. Refuse BadThreshold on a threshold outside zero through sample_max and BadRange on a span outside the samples, each before either channel is mutated and each depending only on the shared threshold or the shared length, else center-clip both channels over the span with the same threshold via ALES87's center clip. It reuses ALES87's CenterClipError by name and ALES87's center clip for the arithmetic, inventing no new fault and no new primitive. The crux stands out as four laws: the stereo center-clip law (each channel equals ALES87's mono center clip with the same threshold byte for byte, every quiet sample silenced and every louder sample passed), the balance / length law (left.len equals right.len after the edit and both hold their starting length, a center clip writing values only), the per-channel odd law (the antisymmetry held under the shared dead zone where the crush and tube broke it, every output either zero or exactly its input, the map idempotent so twice equals once, the ratio held on the passed samples, an identical-channel master staying identical, threshold zero the identity), and the atomicity / degenerate law (any refusal leaves both channels byte for byte untouched and still balanced, threshold zero the identity on both, count zero the identity on both)."
say "ales-stereo-center-clip: Lens TAME — two bounded i16 Clips (left, right) center-clipped in lockstep by one shared dead zone; the balance invariant is asserted on entry and exit, the threshold and span are bound-checked once before any write, and because those checks hold identically for both channels each mono center clip is pre-validated to succeed so no refusal can land between the two channel edits; center_clip walks the span once per channel, taking each magnitude in i32 so the magnitude of sample_min, one past the positive rail, is representable, and writing only zero or the untouched input so there is no rail edge and no saturate, never touching a byte past len so the length holds exactly; it reuses ALES87's center clip per channel over its public API and ALES87's CenterClipError whole, inventing no new primitive; the stereo center-clip law is proven against ALES87's own center clip run per channel, the per-channel odd law proves the out-of-phase field's antisymmetry is held under the shared dead zone, that every output is zero or its input, that the map is idempotent, and that a one-to-two field keeps its ratio on the passed samples, the two refusals leave both channels byte-for-byte untouched, and threshold zero is the identity; siloed to lotus/, no real sample rate, no network, no keys, no funds, no device, no speaker."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/stereo_center_clip"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_center_clip.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-stereo-center-clip: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/stereo_center_clip.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-stereo-center-clip: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-stereo-center-clip: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-center-clip' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-center-clip: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-stereo-center-clip line"
